Fuzix for the Ampro Z80 Littleboard with MDISK

This builds a version of Fuzix for the LB with the n/Systems (TCJ 29/30)
MDISK interface fitted. On this setup there is a lot more memory, and tasks
can be hardware switched but with a 32K size limit.

As the OS doesn't need to be burned into ROM it's built as both a bootstrap
(boot.com) that loads the OS from the SCSI disk, and fuzix.com which is a CP/M
boot of the Fuzix kernel which then takes over the hardware.

Memory Map
0000-7FFF	Switchable EPROM/RAM/Banked RAM
8000-FFFF	Fixed as the second 32K block of memory in the bankable RAM

Kernel

0000-7FFF	Kernel
8000-FFFF	Kernel, Data, Buffers, Common
		IM2 page is start of common

User

0000-7FFF	Process
8000-FFFF	Kernel, Data, Buffers, Common
		IM2 page is start of common

Hardware
-	Z80 DART
-	Z80 CTC. Channels 0 & 1 drive the DART, 2 & 3 free
-	1772 Floppy Disk
-	NCR5380 SCSI
-	Printer port (output/strobe/busy only)
-	MDISK


